            <ArticleTitle>Rib compression of the coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>255-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes the finding of coronary artery narrowing caused by compression by an overlying rib in two patients with cardiomegaly. There is probably no clinical significance to this finding. The primary differential diagnostic entity is myocardial bridging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
